preferred-citation:
  type: report
  title: "Fin-ally Supported: Shark-fin supports for long, flat, tilted overhangs. A hobbyist's field guide and a defensive publication"
  authors:
    - family-names: Armstrong
      given-names: Matthew
      alias: The-Dorkknight
  date-published: "2026-10-19"
  version: "1.0"
  url: "https://github.com/The-Dorkknight/fin-ally-supported"
  abstract: >-
    Shark-fin supports: thin plates that run downhill under a long, flat, tilted overhang, follow its slope,
    touch it only at small teeth (two anchor teeth at the low end), stop at 85 % of its height with a blunt
    flat top, and stand on a crossbar foot and a one-layer brim pad. Includes the method in rebuildable detail,
    the design history with its mistakes, slicer-estimated costs, a test plan, and a defensive disclosure of the
    method and its variations, dedicated to the public. Nothing has been printed yet.
